[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892796813","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569#issuecomment-2892796813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569","id":2892796813,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sbJON","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-20T03:26:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T03:44:25Z","body":"GDScript has a heavy use of HashMap lookups, so I tested with [GaijinEntertainment/godot-das@master/examples/bunnymark](https://github.com/GaijinEntertainment/godot-das/tree/master/examples/bunnymark's?rgh-link-date=2025-04-25T13%3A42%3A24Z)\r\n\r\nAt 1000 bunnies (because 10000 is very unlikely and in most cases deceiving with a result that only comes with that much) ran side-by-side, the max average FPS in one minute:\r\n| Branch      | FPS  |\r\n|-------------|------|\r\n| Reverted PR | 1307 |\r\n| PR          | 1320 |","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892796813/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911244536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569#issuecomment-2911244536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569","id":2911244536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6thhD4","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T06:21:21Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T06:24:50Z","body":"`if` branches can be dodgy as _sometimes_ going the other way to branchless code can be faster. But it depends on hardware and the access patterns. In an ideal world we would check on non-desktop, e.g. low end mobile (possibly even web, just in case?).\r\n\r\nIn this case I asked grok :grin: and it reckons it should be faster on desktop and mobile.\r\n\r\nBTW I do wonder if there will be branch prediction, if this is not called in a tight loop (I don't know the access patterns, and I'm no expert at branch prediction).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911244536/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911930886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569#issuecomment-2911930886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569","id":2911930886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tkIoG","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T10:01:12Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T10:03:28Z","body":"> `if` branches can be dodgy as _sometimes_ going the other way to branchless code can be faster. But it depends on hardware and the access patterns. In an ideal world we would check on non-desktop, e.g. low end mobile (possibly even web, just in case?).\r\n\r\nYes, this definitely feels like a micro optimization - it's hard to intuit that the new code is faster than the old one. I would not have proposed this change if it didn't lead to such major performance differences for lookup.\r\nOn the other hand, branch prediction has been ubiquitously important for CPUs for decades, so we can probably expect `if` to stay extremely fast on consumer hardware.\r\n\r\n> BTW I do wonder if there will be branch prediction, if this is not called in a tight loop (I don't know the access patterns, and I'm no expert at branch prediction).\r\n\r\nYes, branch prediction happens on every branch (even including short-circuiting `&&` and `||`). As far as I've seen, you can normally assume that the branch that is entered most often is the one that will be predicted.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911930886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912821749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569#issuecomment-2912821749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569","id":2912821749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tniH1","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/